      "body": "2 rooms reserved for suspected cases burned before fire was put out, says medical official | Anadolu\nEDITION Africa Residents burn Ebola treatment center in north-central DR Congo 2 rooms reserved for suspected cases burned before fire was put out, says medical official James Tasamba 31 October 2026 • Update : 31 October 2026 KIGALI, Rwanda Persons unknown burned an Ebola treatment center in the Democratic Republic of Congo on Saturday, an official said, amid efforts to contain an outbreak caused by the Bundibugyo virus.\nThe incident took place in Bafwasende, a rural town in the north-central Tsopo province in the early morning, according to Marcel Likilo, a medical doctor in charge of the particular health zone.\nThe incident occurred just one week after mob lynched a health worker while responding to an Ebola alert in the area.",
